<article class="legacy-case" id="obdlink-mx-plus-vs-vlinker-bm-plus"><h3>OBDLink MX+ vs vLinker BM+: Broad Networks or BMW Focus?</h3><p class="legacy-provenance">Research from the former <code>/guides/obdlink-mx-plus-vs-vlinker-bm-plus/</code> comparison, now redirected to this consolidated resource.</p><h4>Map the whole garage first</h4><p>A one-BMW purchase and a mixed-brand garage create different answers. List every current vehicle, likely next vehicle, phone or computer platform and required application before comparing adapter prices.</p>
<h4>Where MX+ reaches beyond the BMW lane</h4><p>OBDLink documents legislated OBD-II support, multiple host platforms, firmware maintenance and added MS-CAN and SW-CAN access. That makes MX+ the more defensible starting point for a garage that includes supported Ford or GM work as well as general diagnostics.</p>
<h4>Where BM+ stays focused</h4><p>Vgate presents BM+ for BMW-oriented applications, and the live BimmerCode or BimmerLink selector controls the exact vehicle path. For an owner who has one supported BMW and no need for the extra networks documented for MX+, that narrower focus can be sufficient.</p><details><summary>View original technical diagrams (2)</summary><figure><picture><source media="(max-width:640px)" srcset="/images/guides/obdlink-mx-plus-vs-vlinker-bm-plus/cs035-visual-a-mobile.svg"/><img src="/images/guides/obdlink-mx-plus-vs-vlinker-bm-plus/cs035-visual-a.svg" alt="OBDLink MX+ vs vLinker BM+: Broad Networks or BMW Focus?: preserved comparison figure 1" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/></picture><figcaption>Original adapter analysis diagram 1; confirm current model and application-level evidence before use.</figcaption></figure>
