<article class="legacy-case" id="vlinker-bm-plus-vs-mc-plus"><h3>vLinker BM+ vs MC+: Which Vgate Adapter Fits Your Apps?</h3><p class="legacy-provenance">Research from the former <code>/guides/vlinker-bm-plus-vs-mc-plus/</code> comparison, now redirected to this consolidated resource.</p><h4>BMW compatibility comes from the app</h4><p>The current BimmerCode adapter list includes both BM+ and MC+ across named BMW-family model groups. That is stronger evidence than a marketplace title, but it still is not permission to skip the vehicle selector. Model year, chassis generation, phone platform, app version and connection method all matter.</p>
<h4>Where the MC+ earns its extra scope</h4><p>Vgate describes MC+ as supporting all legislated OBD-II protocols and highlights HS-CAN and MS-CAN coverage for vehicles such as Ford and GM. That is relevant if the adapter will serve more than a BMW household or an app that explicitly calls for those networks. It does not make MC+ automatically better for BimmerCode.</p>
<h4>Price is a snapshot, not the decision</h4><p>On September 1, 2026, Vgate's store showed BM+ at $47.99 sale / $68 regular and MC+ at $66.99 sale / $69.99 regular. Currency, tax, shipping, promotions and regional inventory can change. Recheck both official product pages at purchase time.</p><details><summary>View original technical diagrams (2)</summary><figure><picture><source media="(max-width:640px)" srcset="/images/guides/vlinker-bm-plus-vs-mc-plus/cs-037-app-and-protocol-fit-mobile.svg"/><img src="/images/guides/vlinker-bm-plus-vs-mc-plus/cs-037-app-and-protocol-fit.svg" alt="vLinker BM+ vs MC+: Which Vgate Adapter Fits Your Apps?: preserved comparison figure 1" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/></picture><figcaption>Original adapter analysis diagram 1; confirm current model and application-level evidence before use.</figcaption></figure>
